PSYCHOPY INTEGRATION NOTES
==========================

PsychoPy version used: 2026.1.3
Main experiment file  : Sandhi_Demo/Sandi_Interface_All_Trials_lastrun.py

DO NOT run the _lastrun.py file directly for EEG sessions.
Use the launcher instead:
    python Sandhi_Demo/run_experiment.py

What the launcher adds that the raw _lastrun.py does not have
-------------------------------------------------------------
  1. EEG stream verification before the PsychoPy window opens.
  2. Operator prompt to confirm LabRecorder is recording.
  3. Optional muselsl auto-start (--start-muselsl flag).

Current marker implementation in _lastrun.py (known issue)
-----------------------------------------------------------
  The existing EEG_Start_Code block uses:
    channel_format='string'
    push_sample(['experiment_start'])  <- string labels

  The architecture calls for integer codes (int32) so that LabRecorder
  saves numeric event markers directly usable by EEGLab / MNE.

  To fix this, in PsychoPy Builder:
    1. Open Sandi_Interface_All_Trials.psyexp.
    2. In the "EEG_Start_Code" code component (Before Experiment tab),
       replace the existing StreamInfo block with:
         from eeg_lsl_bridge import SandhiMarkerOutlet, MARKERS
         marker_outlet = SandhiMarkerOutlet()
    3. Replace every  marker_outlet.push_sample(['<string>'])  call with
       the corresponding integer code, e.g.:
         marker_outlet.push(MARKERS.EXPERIMENT_START)
         marker_outlet.push(MARKERS.EMOCIONES_TRIAL_START)
         ... etc.
    4. Re-export to _lastrun.py from Builder.

  The full marker code table is defined in software/eeg_lsl_bridge.py
  under the MARKERS class.

piloting flag
-------------
  The pilot data files confirm the experiment was run with piloting=True
  (auto-set by PsychoPy Builder when running from the GUI without the
  --session flag). For formal data collection runs, launch via:
    python Sandhi_Demo/run_experiment.py
  This invokes the script as __main__ and sets piloting=False by default.

Randomization seed
------------------
  TrialHandler2 is called with seed=None in all three task loops. This means
  trial order is not reproducible across runs. For counterbalancing or
  reproducibility, pass an explicit seed tied to the participant ID, e.g.:
    seed=int(expInfo['participant'])
